HYBRID_RESULT {"hybrid": "H01", "parents": ["S01", "S02"], "synthesis": "**AX-731 Cross-Domain Electrical-Mechanical Relations Engineering Synthesis**\n\n**Electrical Specifications:**\n- **Nominal DC Bus Voltage:** 540 volts [C01]\n- **Continuous Current Rating:** 18 amperes [C02]\n- **Overcurrent Trip Threshold:** 24 amperes [C03]\n\n**Deductions:**\n- The system is designed to operate with a nominal DC bus voltage of 540 volts.\n- The continuous current rating of 18 amperes is the maximum current the system can handle continuously without overheating or damaging the components.\n- The overcurrent trip threshold of 24 amperes is set to protect the system from excessive current, which is 33.33% higher than the continuous current rating, providing a safety margin to prevent overcurrent conditions.\n\n**Mechanical Specifications:**\n- **Actuator Output", "readouts": [{"id": "S01", "raw": "The AX-731 electrical technical specifications, numbers, and conditions available in the memory are as follows:\n\n- **Nominal DC Bus Voltage:** 540 volts [C01]\n- **Continuous Current Rating:** 18 amperes [C02]\n- **Overcurrent Trip Threshold:** 24 amperes [C03]\n\n**Deductions:**\n- The system is designed to operate with a nominal DC bus voltage of 540 volts.\n- The continuous current rating of 18 amperes is the maximum current the system can handle continuously without overheating or damaging the components.\n- The overcurrent trip threshold of 24 amperes is set to protect the system from excessive current, which is 33.33% higher than the continuous current rating, providing a safety margin to prevent overcurrent conditions.", "question": "List all AX-731 electrical technical specifications, numbers and conditions in the available memory.", "role": "domain"}, {"id": "S02", "raw": "The AX-731 mechanical technical specifications, numbers, and conditions available in the memory are as follows:\n\n- **Actuator Output Torque**: 12 newton meters. [C04]\n- **Gearbox Reduction Ratio**: 5 to 1. [C05]\n- **Maximum Mechanical Axis Speed**: 1200 rpm. [C06]\n\n**Deductions**:\n- Given the gearbox reduction ratio of 5 to 1, the input speed to the gearbox must be higher than the output speed. If the maximum mechanical axis speed (output speed) is 1200 rpm, the input speed to the gearbox would be 1200 rpm * 5 = 6000 rpm. However, this deduction is not explicitly stated in the provided information.", "question": "List all AX-731 mechanical technical specifications, numbers and conditions in the available memory.", "role": "domain"}, {"id": "C01", "raw": "The AX-731 nominal DC bus voltage is 540 volts.", "question": "What is the AX-731 nominal DC bus voltage?", "role": "original evidence"}, {"id": "C02", "raw": "The AX-731 continuous current rating is 18 amperes.", "question": "What is the AX-731 continuous current rating?", "role": "original evidence"}, {"id": "C03", "raw": "The AX-731 overcurrent trip threshold is 24 amperes.", "question": "What is the AX-731 overcurrent trip threshold?", "role": "original evidence"}, {"id": "C04", "raw": "The AX-731 actuator rated output torque is 12 newton meters.", "question": "What is the AX-731 actuator rated output torque?", "role": "original evidence"}, {"id": "C05", "raw": "The AX-731 gearbox reduction ratio is 5 to 1.", "question": "What is the AX-731 gearbox reduction ratio?", "role": "original evidence"}, {"id": "C06", "raw": "The AX-731 maximum mechanical axis speed is 1200 rpm.", "question": "What is the AX-731 maximum mechanical axis speed?", "role": "original evidence"}], "hybrid_questions": [{"question": "How does the AX-731 drive continuous current rating compare to its overcurrent trip threshold?", "raw": "The continuous current rating of the AX-731 is 18 amperes, while the overcurrent trip threshold is 24 amperes. This means the overcurrent trip threshold is 33.33% higher than the continuous current rating, providing a safety margin to prevent overcurrent conditions.", "unknown": false}, {"question": "Which electrical and mechanical specifications describe the AX-731 drive and actuator together?", "raw": "The electrical and mechanical specifications that describe the AX-731 drive and actuator together are as follows:\n\n**Electrical Specifications:**\n- **Nominal DC Bus Voltage:** 540 volts [C01]\n- **Continuous Current Rating:** 18 amperes [C02]\n- **Overcurrent Trip Threshold:** 24 amperes [C03]\n\n**Mechanical Specifications:**\n- **Actuator Output:** (The document does not provide specific details about the actuator output, so this information is UNKNOWN.)\n\nThe electrical specifications provide details about the voltage and current ratings, while the mechanical specifications are incomplete in the provided information.", "unknown": false}], "leaf_probes": [{"id": "C01", "expected": "540 volts", "raw": "The nominal DC bus voltage for the AX-731 is 540 volts.", "hit": true}, {"id": "C02", "expected": "18 amperes", "raw": "The AX-731 continuous current rating is 18 amperes.", "hit": true}, {"id": "C03", "expected": "24 amperes", "raw": "The overcurrent trip threshold for the AX-731 is 24 amperes.", "hit": true}, {"id": "C04", "expected": "12 newton meters", "raw": "UNKNOWN. The provided information does not include the actuator rated output torque for the AX-731.", "hit": false}, {"id": "C05", "expected": "5 to 1", "raw": "UNKNOWN. The provided information does not include the gearbox reduction ratio for the AX-731.", "hit": false}, {"id": "C06", "expected": "1200 rpm", "raw": "UNKNOWN. The provided information does not include the maximum mechanical axis speed for the AX-731.", "hit": false}], "leaf_hits": 3}
