HYBRID_RESULT {"hybrid": "H02", "parents": ["S02", "S03"], "synthesis": "**Integrated Technical Memory for AX-731 Cross-Domain Mechanical-Software Relations Engineering Synthesis**\n\n### Mechanical Specifications\n- **Actuator Output Torque**: 12 newton meters. [C04]\n- **Gearbox Reduction Ratio**: 5 to 1. [C05]\n- **Maximum Mechanical Axis Speed**: 1200 rpm. [C06]\n\n### Software Specifications\n- **Sampling Interval**: The AX-731 PLC samples the drive current every 10 milliseconds. [C07]\n- **Fault Code F17**: The fault code F17 is raised when the AX-731 drive current exceeds 24 amperes. [C08]\n- **Reset Procedure for F17**: After fault F17 is triggered, a manual reset is required. This reset should only be performed after the drive current has returned to a level below the threshold", "readouts": [{"id": "S02", "raw": "The AX-731 mechanical technical specifications, numbers, and conditions available in the memory are as follows:\n\n- **Actuator Output Torque**: 12 newton meters. [C04]\n- **Gearbox Reduction Ratio**: 5 to 1. [C05]\n- **Maximum Mechanical Axis Speed**: 1200 rpm. [C06]\n\n**Deductions**:\n- Given the gearbox reduction ratio of 5 to 1, the input speed to the gearbox must be higher than the output speed. If the maximum mechanical axis speed (output speed) is 1200 rpm, the input speed to the gearbox would be 1200 rpm * 5 = 6000 rpm. However, this deduction is not explicitly stated in the provided information.", "question": "List all AX-731 mechanical technical specifications, numbers and conditions in the available memory.", "role": "domain"}, {"id": "S03", "raw": "The technical specifications, numbers, and conditions for the AX-731 software, as available in the memory, are as follows:\n\n- **Sampling Interval**: The AX-731 PLC samples the drive current every 10 milliseconds. [C07]\n- **Fault Code F17**: The fault code F17 is raised when the AX-731 drive current exceeds 24 amperes. [C08]\n- **Reset Procedure for F17**: After fault F17 is triggered, a manual reset is required. This reset should only be performed after the drive current has returned to a level below the threshold of 24 amperes. [C09]", "question": "List all AX-731 software technical specifications, numbers and conditions in the available memory.", "role": "domain"}, {"id": "C04", "raw": "The AX-731 actuator rated output torque is 12 newton meters.", "question": "What is the AX-731 actuator rated output torque?", "role": "original evidence"}, {"id": "C05", "raw": "The AX-731 gearbox reduction ratio is 5 to 1.", "question": "What is the AX-731 gearbox reduction ratio?", "role": "original evidence"}, {"id": "C06", "raw": "The AX-731 maximum mechanical axis speed is 1200 rpm.", "question": "What is the AX-731 maximum mechanical axis speed?", "role": "original evidence"}, {"id": "C07", "raw": "The AX-731 PLC samples the drive current every 10 milliseconds.", "question": "How often does the AX-731 PLC sample drive current?", "role": "original evidence"}, {"id": "C08", "raw": "The fault code raised when the AX-731 drive current exceeds 24 amperes is F17.", "question": "What fault code is raised when AX-731 drive current exceeds 24 amperes?", "role": "original evidence"}, {"id": "C09", "raw": "The reset required after AX-731 fault F17 is a manual reset. This reset should be performed after the current returns below the threshold.", "question": "What reset is required after AX-731 fault F17?", "role": "original evidence"}], "hybrid_questions": [{"question": "What does the AX-731 PLC do when current exceeds 24 amperes, and what reset is required?", "raw": "When the drive current exceeds 24 amperes, the AX-731 PLC raises the fault code F17. After fault F17 is triggered, a manual reset is required. This reset should only be performed after the drive current has returned to a level below the threshold.", "unknown": false}, {"question": "Which mechanical axis speed and PLC current monitoring interval are specified for AX-731?", "raw": "The specified maximum mechanical axis speed for the AX-731 is 1200 rpm, and the PLC current monitoring interval is every 10 milliseconds.", "unknown": false}], "leaf_probes": [{"id": "C04", "expected": "12 newton meters", "raw": "The AX-731 actuator rated output torque is 12 newton meters. [C04]", "hit": true}, {"id": "C05", "expected": "5 to 1", "raw": "The gearbox reduction ratio for the AX-731 is 5 to 1. [C05]", "hit": true}, {"id": "C06", "expected": "1200 rpm", "raw": "The maximum mechanical axis speed of the AX-731 is 1200 rpm. [C06]", "hit": true}, {"id": "C07", "expected": "10 milliseconds", "raw": "The AX-731 PLC samples the drive current every 10 milliseconds. [C07]", "hit": true}, {"id": "C08", "expected": "F17", "raw": "The fault code F17 is raised when the AX-731 drive current exceeds 24 amperes.", "hit": true}, {"id": "C09", "expected": "manual reset", "raw": "After fault F17 is triggered on the AX-731, a manual reset is required. This reset should only be performed after the drive current has returned to a level below the threshold.", "hit": true}], "leaf_hits": 6}
